EXTENSION "ARMDef_The_Sundered_Eagle_Anatolia_SyagricusOfHouseJerbiton" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Sundered Eagle - Syagricus of House Jerbiton"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_The_Sundered_Eagle_Core_Ext"

    # Syagricus of House Jerbiton (Chapter Eight: Anatolia, p117): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #t5e3d74c6362cd655dac711 ^"Syagricus of House Jerbiton" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t971f29fc8b8b7dfe6c00c7 ^"Moero’s Garden"]
            ^"Age" STRING "102 (Apparent Age: 43)"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Outspoken +3, Opinionated +2, Kind +1"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Sundered Eagle"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 117
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Syagricus is the oddest Jerbiton member of the covenant, both in temperament and physically. He is a genuine hermaphrodite and seems quite proud of it. He dresses to accentuate both his male and female gender, wearing a full beard and a dress that accentuates his bust. His sexual nature is inexplicable but medically proven, and Syagricus sees his true nature as beautiful and refuses to hide it. His sodales are very accepting of his nature, but would prefer he didn’t mention it as much as he does.\n\nSyagricus happily imbibes his Longevity Ritual, which is a daily mixture of specially prepared herbs and powders drunk at noon, and is hale and hearty. Interested in art, etiquette, and a pleasant life, much like his sodales, he is more determined to regain the covenant’s objects of art lost when they fled Constantinople than in continuing a hedonistic lifestyle. Syagricus has joined Valnastium’s league of New Iconophiles (*Houses of Hermes: Soceitates*, page 54), and travels to Constantinople at least once a year to search for the lost pieces of art.\n\nSyagricus’ apprentice, Pancratius, is due to be gauntleted in 1221, and hopes to receive the honor at the upcoming Tribunal. Pancratius will likely join Moero’s Garden as a full member, and Trasaric and Helladius hope that he will side with them in assisting the emperor, tipping the vote in their favor."
    }

}
